(ned m22 -- per-fork FETCH from the RACK CAL table.deployed 2026-08-04)
o<m22> sub
#<p> = #1
(FORK COUNT IS #3973, NOT A LITERAL. Operator 2026-08-16 added T15 and)
(could not GET TOOL: the guard below refused pocket 15 outright. #3973 is)
(the count [ATC]POCKETS carries and the GUI reads. Fallback 14 only if the)
(var is unset, which would otherwise refuse EVERY pocket.)
#<nmax> = #3973
o100 if [#<nmax> LT 1]
  #<nmax> = 14
o100 endif
o101 if [[#<p> LT 1] OR [#<p> GT #<nmax>]]
  (abort, m22: pocket #<p> outside 1..#<nmax>)
o101 endif
#<base>  = [4100 + [#<p> * 4]]
o102 if [[#[#<base> + 3] NE 1] OR [ABS[#[#<base> + 2]] LT 0.001]]
  (abort, m22: fork #<p> has no complete RACK CAL data - run RACK CALIBRATION)
o102 endif
o103 if [[#[4107] NE 1] OR [ABS[#[4106]] LT 0.001]]
  (abort, m22: P1 has no RACK CAL data - Z heights are defined relative to P1)
o103 endif
#<sx>  = #[#<base>]
#<sy>  = #[#<base> + 1]
#<dz>  = [#[#<base> + 2] - #[4106]]
#<zload> = [#3981 + #<dz>]
#<zappr> = [#3982 + #<dz>]
(exit clearance: the INCOMING tool's SAFETY X when set; see m21 note)
#<tin> = #[4000 + #<p>]
#<tsx> = 0
o106 if [[#<tin> GE 1] AND [#<tin> LE #<nmax>]]
  #<tsx> = #[4200 + [2 * #<tin>]]
o106 endif
o107 if [#<tsx> GT 0.01]
  #<cx> = [#<sx> - #<tsx>]
o107 else
  #<cx> = [#<sx> + [#3987 - #3983]]
o107 endif
#<ztrav> = #3974
(TRAVERSE = 8000 mm/min, operator 2026-08-16: "when i use the ATC tool)
(change, the traverse is too slow. it can be 8000mm/min". Set HERE, in the)
(file, not on the rack page -- #3976 is PB's ATC USER 3 spare and the)
(production team must not be dialling tool-change feeds.)
(HEADROOM: AXIS_Z max is 10158 mm/min and AXIS_X/Y 12000, so 8000 clears)
(both. Feed override still scales it, as asked.)
(HISTORY: this briefly ran at 0.80 of axis max and was reverted when joint)
(following errors appeared. The second rtapi_app SIGSEGV then happened with)
(the revert already in place, so the speed was not the cause -- the crash)
(signature is the hm2_eth packet loss documented in ned_brain.py:1478.)
#<ftravxy> = 8000
#<ftrav>   = 8000
o105 if [#<ztrav> LT #<zappr>]
  (abort, m22: traverse Z is below the approach height for fork #<p>)
o105 endif
M66 P0 L0
o80 if [#5399 GT 0]
  (abort, m22: a tool is still clamped - refusing to descend onto the fork)
o80 endif
G90
(entry height. #<_rack_between>=1 means m21 just emptied the spindle inside)
(the rack zone - enter at approach+50 instead of the full traverse Z. Gated)
(by BOTH the sensor - o80 above proved nothing is clamped - and the logic)
(record #3991, operator 2026-08-04. Flag is consumed either way; a fetch)
(arriving from the workspace has flag 0 and enters at traverse Z as before.)
#<zin> = #<ztrav>
o88 if [EXISTS[#<_rack_between>]]
  o90 if [[#<_rack_between> GT 0] AND [#3991 EQ 0]]
    #<zin> = [#<zappr> + 50.0]
    o92 if [#<zin> GT 0]
      #<zin> = 0
    o92 endif
  o90 endif
o88 endif
#<_rack_between> = 0
G1 G53 F[#<ftrav>] Z[#<zin>]
G1 G53 F[#<ftravxy>] X[#<sx>] Y[#<sy>]
G1 G53 F[#<ftrav>] Z[#<zappr>]
M24
G1 G53 F[#3980] Z[#<zload>]
M25
M66 P0 L0
o81 if [#5399 LT 1]
  (abort, m22: tool-LOCKED never asserted after M25 - NOT pulling out of the fork)
o81 endif
M66 P1 L0
o82 if [#5399 GT 0]
  (abort, m22: tool-RELEASED still asserted - drawbar not shut, NOT pulling out)
o82 endif
(BOOKKEEPING HERE -- grip is proven by the gates above, so the tool IS in)
(the spindle whatever happens next. #<tool> read from the rack map for this)
(pocket, which the put-away keeps true.)
#<tool> = #[4000 + #<p>]
#3991 = #<tool>
#[4000 + #<p>] = 0
M61 Q#<tool>
(DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"rackatc"}.store_tool{#<p>, 0}])
G1 G53 F[#3980] X[#<cx>]
G1 G53 F[#<ftrav>] Z[#<ztrav>]
o<m22> endsub
M2
